<title>BELGIUM: EU to start Spain, Portugal grain tenders Feb 6.</title>
<headline>EU to start Spain, Portugal grain tenders Feb 6.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Adjudications will start on February 6 on tenders for preferential imports of 850,000 tonnes of maize and 150,000 tonnes of sorghum into Spain and 350,000 tonnes of maize into Portugal, the European Commission said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>Bids for the first tender can be placed from January 31 and the final Spanish maize and sorghum tenders will be on February 27, said the EU Official Journal.</p>
<p>The Portuguese maize tender is due to close on March 13.</p>
<p>The tenders are for grain traditionally imported from the United States at lower than normal tariffs as part of a decade-old trade agreement to compensate U.S. exporters for losses after Spain and Portugal joined the EU in 1986.</p>
<p>Import licences will be valid for 50 days from the date of issue.</p>
<p>-Brussels Bureau +322 287 6830</p>
</text>
